[h1]Taoist — v6.2.0[/h1]
A [b]hardcore rework[/b] of the base game: a living world, a harsh economy, towns you can rule, families, lifelong storylines, tougher battles, new paths of cultivation, houses of your own, and now [b]cultivator clans with their elders[/b].
Most features can be tuned or turned off in [b]S&M Configs[/b] (title screen). The harder your settings, the higher your S&M score and the better your rewards. If it gets too hard, combine it with other mods.
Give me a like to let me know it is useful, thanks! If you want to support the work: [url=https://ko-fi.com/fouru]Ko-fi[/url]
News, questions and bug reports: join the [url=https://discord.gg/XKaP3EYfw]Discord server[/url]!

[h2]⚠ Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3385996759]Fouru's ModLib[/url] v2.3.07 or newer
[*][b]Move ModLib to the TOP of your mod list[/b], then [b]restart the game[/b].
[/list]

[h2]★ New in 6.2[/h2]
[b]Choose your destinies[/b]
[list]
[*]Character creation: a new window with every innate destiny of the game, sorted by quality and name, with filters by quality, name and description
[*]Take as many as you like, on top of the 3 you roll. Each one lowers the S&M score of the new save (3,000 to 8,000 P by quality): power has its price
[/list]
[b]Taoist × Dao of Creation[/b] (optional: only when you play both mods)
[list]
[*]2 new storylines: [b]The Nameless Art[/b], an outcast who invents a martial art and the sect that wants it back; [b]For One Heir Only[/b], a dying master, one last art and two candidates
[*]Characters create martial arts of their own and teach them to you, and 9 endings of the older storylines reward you with an art or Dao Essence
[*]The options of Dao of Creation have their own page in S&M Configs
[/list]
[b]Also[/b]: Taoist wallpapers for the title screen (Change Theme); trainer teleport by area; windows of several mods no longer open over each other.

[h2]New in 6.1[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Clan elders[/b]: outsiders who guard a clan for a salary, vote on its wars and fight in them. A disloyal one may flee, or [b]betray its clan in the middle of the battle[/b]
[*][b]Succession[/b]: when the head of a clan dies, the family carries on. A clan wiped out leaves its mansion in ruins
[*]Faster months, S&M score balance, new windows for plots, clans and elders, an option to hide the "Damage Calc" button (F9 still opens it)
[/list]

[h2]New in 6.0[/h2]
[b]Five new paths of cultivation[/b] (buttons on the cultivation screen, each one can be turned off in S&M Configs)
[list]
[*][b]Body Refining[/b]: Copper Skin → Iron Bone → Jade Marrow → Golden Body → Undying Body. Temper your flesh with the blows you take, training and medicinal baths: max HP, defense, fist / palm / finger. Train under waterfalls, in lava and thunder pools, and face the body tribulation. Some sects teach it, and NPCs walk the path too
[*][b]Merit and Karma[/b]: good deeds bring merit (attack, defense, luck, gifts from the grateful, kinder NPCs, softer lightning). Evil deeds bring karma: more attack, less defense, bounties and revenge... and the evil way: [b]massacre a town[/b] in a real battle and leave it in ruins for 10 years
[*][b]Artisan Dao[/b]: alchemy, forging, talismans, feng shui, herbs and mining as 6 crafts with ranks, guild exams, masterpieces, commissions from NPCs and apprentices. Every area has mine veins and herb valleys to stay in for years
[*][b]Dao Heart[/b]: the steadiness of your mind (max SP / MP, beating heart demons), shaken by betrayal and broken promises
[*][b]Spirit Sense[/b]: max SP, senses ambushes and lowers heart demons. Scan your surroundings once a month: cultivators around (portraits, the hostile ones), herbs, ores and the nearest places
[/list]
[b]Estates[/b]
[list]
[*]Every town has its own map of plots in districts, mortals who live and grow, and a palace for the town master
[*]Buy land or a mortal's house, build from a thatched hut up to an immortal palace, and add rooms: quiet room, training ground, herb garden, spirit gathering array, ancestral hall
[*]House tax every month (unpaid tax: the house is taken back). NPCs buy houses too, and families live together
[/list]
[b]Also[/b]
[list]
[*]4 new storylines (16 in all): Old Tie's Forge, The House on the Old Street, Ashes of the Town, A Heartbeat in the Stone
[*]S&M Configs: options for the paths and estates (on/off, gain rates, prices, tax); storylines on a page of their own
[*]Rebirth button moved to the player info. Many fixes
[/list]

[h2]Features in short[/h2]
[b]New game[/b]: starting divine artifacts, destinies of your choice, skip the intro, roles for the player and NPCs (Power, Speed, Tao, Atk, Def, Angel, Evil, Merchant), S&M presets (Level 0-10), one-life mode, in-game trainer.

[b]S&M score[/b]: every setting is worth points; the score changes battle exp and loot (-20% to +50%), gives a title and a start bonus, and is recorded for every character.

[b]Storylines[/b]: 16 NPC storylines (18 with Dao of Creation) with portraits, real battles, several acts, time limits and endings (Cold Sword, Hundred-Year Wager, Roadside Inn, Heart Demon...). Failed acts open another path, and the lines remember each other.

[b]World and NPCs[/b]: NPCs grow, craft, earn titles, take dao companions and have children. Hire a team, NPCs join your battles, stalkers chase rare items, random encounters, reworked dramas, quests and commissions.

[b]Families and legacy[/b]: household upkeep, family accounts, family tree; when you die, play on as your child or grandchild.

[b]Economy[/b]: inflation and currency reform, bank accounts and storage fees, bank loans with debt collectors, a player market with NPCs (negotiation, barter, buy orders), sect contribution exchange.

[b]Towns[/b]: budgets, taxes, town masters and guardians, bounties and wanted hunters, your own house, cultivator clans with their elders, feuds and clan wars.

[b]Cultivation[/b]: long seclusions while the world keeps living, Qi cultivation, spirit stone cultivation, natural breakthroughs, rebirth, time skips.

[b]Battle[/b]: mana shields, special and growing monsters, reworked damage with block / evade / crit, the [b]Damage Calc[/b] window (F9), losses on defeat, refining of rings, outfits, artifacts and mounts, several divine artifacts with hotkeys.

[b]Interface[/b]: Taoist Settings, the Taoist log (month by month), icons in texts, optional hidden battle map / previews / damage multiplier / Damage Calc button.

[b]Languages[/b]: English, Chinese (Simplified and Traditional), Korean, Japanese, Vietnamese, Thai, Russian, German, French, Spanish, Latin, plus a custom language system.

